From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:23:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] svga: keep the contents of imported surfaces

svga_texture_from_handle() leaves surface_state at
SVGA_SURFACE_STATE_CREATED. The first time a render target view is made
for the texture, svga_validate_surface_view() takes that to mean the
surface holds nothing yet and sends SVGA3D_InvalidateGBSurface for it,
which throws away what the buffer contains.

An imported surface was created, and usually filled, by someone else, so
its contents are not ours to drop. The Android EGL platform makes this
visible: it imports the gralloc buffer it dequeued as a new DRI image on
every frame (get_back_bo()), so every frame starts from an invalidated
buffer while eglQuerySurface(EGL_BUFFER_AGE_EXT) still reports the age the
buffer queue tracks. hwui trusts that age and redraws only the damaged
region, and the rest of the window comes out black. Seen with Waydroid
(Android 11, Mesa 23.2.1) on VirtualBox VMSVGA with a VGPU10 device: with
this change Files and Settings draw fully with buffer age on; without
it only the region drawn last is shown.

Mark level 0 of an imported texture as defined and its surface state as
UPDATED, as for a texture whose contents came from an upload.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_resource_texture.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_resource_texture.c b/src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_resource_texture.c
index 8ce5b94..403f8a0 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_resource_texture.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_resource_texture.c
@@ -1213,6 +1213,14 @@ svga_texture_from_handle(struct pipe_screen *screen,
 
    tex->imported = true;
 
+   /* The surface was created and filled by someone else. Mark it as holding
+    * content, so that rendering to it does not first invalidate it: that
+    * discards what is there, and EGL platforms that re-import the same
+    * buffer every frame (Android) rely on it surviving for buffer age.
+    */
+   svga_define_texture_level(tex, 0, 0);
+   tex->surface_state = SVGA_SURFACE_STATE_UPDATED;
+
    ss->hud.num_resources++;
 
    return &tex->b;
